Stop an idle window's display link; gpui's frame waker restarts it

This change applies to zed-industries/zed 90d8514059561f0e44af0a32e84e1c329cef3232
after patches/0001–0005.

What it does:
- MacWindow implements `PlatformWindow::frame_waker` and `schedule_frame`,
  gpui's hooks for platforms that stop requesting frames for idle
  windows. The invalidator calls the waker whenever a window becomes
  dirty and whenever frame demand arises without dirt (next-frame
  callbacks, a throttled frame, a window dirtied again mid-draw);
  `schedule_frame` follows every effect flush that leaves a window dirty
  or owing a present. Either marks a frame requested. A window whose
  display link is idle restarts it and ticks on the next main-queue
  turn, unless an input event presented within the last 8 ms.
- A tick whose frame neither presented nor asked for another stops the
  link. Presenting keeps it, so gpui's one second of presents after
  high-rate input still lands every refresh.
- A CVDisplayLink started within ~3 ms of its next callback slot skips
  it and first fires a refresh later; ticking at once keeps a background
  update from landing a refresh late.
- `examples/idle_frame.rs` (fork-owned, not in this file) checks both:
  an idle panel's main thread stays asleep, and a notify from a
  background task draws before the display link's next tick would have.

Applied cleanly onto 90d8514 after 0001–0005. display_link.rs keeps
is_running after the frame journal's signal.take in stop. Host time
stays objc2_core_video::CVGetCurrentHostTime / CVGetHostClockFrequency
(#65058); this patch does not touch those calls. window.rs frame()
still stops the idle link and still passes signal_at / signal_source
from WindowFrameSource::take_signal. #65059's display-changed callback
is outside this hunk. rustfmt (1.98.1, edition 2024) makes no further
changes.

Re-apply on a roll: git apply --3way patches/0006-idle-display-link.patch
